---
// /accessibility/ (rebuild plan Part 5: "Ship a real /accessibility/
// statement"). Each claim names the code or decision that makes it true.
// Keep it true: when a claim stops holding, change the page in the same PR.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base short="Accessibility"
      description="How we build this site so everyone can use it, where it still falls short, and how to tell us about a problem.">
  <!-- Copy drafted with AI assistance; needs MCO staff review before launch (UM AI disclosure). -->
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>

    {/* University of Montana policy, WCAG 2.1 AA: rebuild plan Part 5;
        CLAUDE.md. */}
    <p>
      We want this site to work for everyone, including people who use a screen reader, or a keyboard
      in place of a mouse. We build it to the Web Content Accessibility
      Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA, which is the standard University of Montana policy sets for
      its websites. Anyone who finds something that does not work can <a href="#report">let us know</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How the site is built</h2>
    <ul>
      {/* src/layouts/Base.astro: .mco-skip-link to <main id="main">. */}
      <li>Every page starts with a link that skips to the main content.</li>
      {/* Header theme button, MCO.initThemeToggle({ cycle: true }); theme
          contract in CLAUDE.md: URL, then saved choice, then light by default
          (DECISIONS D29, data-theme-default in Base.astro). */}
      <li>
        The button in the header switches between light, dark and high contrast themes. The site
        opens in the light theme and remembers a theme once someone picks one.
      </li>
      {/* Kit :focus-visible ring (HOUSE-STYLE §5.4); keyboard checks in the
          kit verify harness, run in CI (verify.config.mjs). */}
      <li>Links and controls work from the keyboard, with a visible focus outline.</li>
      {/* src/scripts/photo-hero.ts and src/scripts/search.ts, MCO.announce. */}
      <li>
        When part of a page changes without reloading, as the homepage photo or search results do,
        screen readers announce the change.
      </li>
      {/* src/pages/mesonet/{stations,status}/index.astro: <caption>, scope. */}
      <li>Station data is laid out in real HTML tables, with captions and header cells.</li>
      {/* Status words: src/pages/mesonet/status/index.astro ("Status and
          health are always words; colour carries nothing"). Underlined
          links: src/styles/site.css. */}
      <li>
        Colour never carries meaning on its own. A station's status is always written out in words,
        and links in a sentence are underlined.
      </li>
      {/* PhotoHero alt text "Looking <direction> from <station>". */}
      <li>Each station photo has a text description naming the station and the direction the camera faces.</li>
      {/* Kit reduced-motion rules (HOUSE-STYLE §5.3). */}
      <li>Animation stops for anyone who has turned on reduced motion on their device.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we test it</h2>
    {/* DECISIONS D17: axe on every PR in all three themes at both widths;
        Lighthouse accessibility budget 100; deploy needs the checks to pass.
        scripts/check-built.mjs (one h1). */}
    <p>
      Before any change goes live, automated tests run it through the axe accessibility checker in all
      three themes, at desktop and phone widths, and through Lighthouse. If a test fails, the change
      does not go live.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it falls short</h2>
    <ul>
      {/* Tools are separate repos and hosts: phase-0-report §3.1. */}
      <li>
        The Mesonet tools, the Station Dashboard and the Snowpack Explorer are separate sites. They
        share this site's design and themes, but each keeps its own theme setting, so a theme picked
        here does not follow a visitor to them.
      </li>
      {/* phase-0-report §3.2: D³ has no h1, main, header or footer; checked
          live again 22 Oct 2026 (no <h1>, no <main>). */}
      <li>
        The D³ Drought Data Dashboard is a separate site with its own design. It does not have a main
        heading or page landmarks yet, which makes it harder to move around with a screen reader.
      </li>
      {/* sustainable-fsa.com/lfp-explorer: Sustainable FSA's own design
          system (phase-0-report §3.2). */}
      <li>The LFP Explorer belongs to the Sustainable FSA project and follows that project's design.</li>
      <li>Photo descriptions name the station and the direction, but they do not describe what is in the picture.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="report">Reporting a problem</h2>
    {/* The footer contact (rebuild plan Phase 1 item 3). */}
    <p>
      Problems go to <a href="mailto:state.climatologist@umontana.edu">state.climatologist@umontana.edu</a>.
      It helps us most to have the page address and a sentence on what wasn't working. The same address
      handles requests for anything on this site in another format.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
